1815	1887	1800	1800	she	24	“ How good it was in you , my dear Mr. Bennet ! But I knew I should persuade you at last . I was sure you loved your girls too well to neglect such an acquaintance . Well , how pleased I am ! and it is such a good joke , too , that you should have gone this morning and never said a word about it till now . ”
1888	1902	1904	1905	Mr. Bennet	2	“ Now , Kitty , you may cough as much as you choose , ”
1926	1936	1938	1938	she	24	“ What an excellent father you have , girls ! ”
1946	2032	1938	1938	she	24	“ I do not know how you will ever make him amends for his kindness ; or me , either , for that matter . At our time of life it is not so pleasant , I can tell you , to be making new acquaintances every day ; but for your sakes , we would do anything . Lydia , my love , though you _ are _ the youngest , I dare say Mr. Bingley will dance with you at the next ball . ”
